# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext" "The fence labels the seed writes read the way Train R relies on"

# Train R labels every fence in the boot seed by what it holds: `memetic-wikitext` for any
# wikitext specimen (memetic is a superset of TiddlyWiki wikitext, so one label covers both),
# `toml meta` for the meta block, `text` for illustration read raw on purpose. And a fence's tick
# run exceeds the longest run inside it, so a closer is never confused with a value.

```memetic-wikitext
<<~ set lares=`aim` from=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/x` to=`?`>>
#   ^^^ keyword.control.sigil.memetic-wikitext
#                         ^^^ support.constant.scheme.lar.memetic-wikitext
```
#<- punctuation.definition.raw.markup.end.tiddlywiki5

```toml meta
title = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot"
#^^^^ source.toml.tw5-syntax
```

```text
<<~ set from=`lar:///a.b.c`>>
#   ^^^ - keyword.control.sigil.memetic-wikitext
#             ^^^ - support.constant.scheme.lar.memetic-wikitext
```

# A FOUR-TICK FENCE holds a three-tick value mid-line and a paired three-tick fence, keeps reading
# its label's grammar after the inner fence closes, and closes only at four.

````memetic-wikitext
\procedure ~stance(named:"philosopher") <$text text=```~ stance named=`$(named)$` ```/>
#                                                                      ^^ keyword.other.variable.substitute-variable.begin.tiddlywiki5
```text
an inner fence, paired, read raw inside the outer one
```
<<~ stance named=`poet`>>
#   ^^^^^^ keyword.control.sigil.memetic-wikitext
````
#<- punctuation.definition.raw.markup.end.tiddlywiki5

After the fence.
#^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ - meta.codeblock.tiddlywiki5

# AN INFO STRING MAY OPEN WITH BLANKS: TiddlyWiki takes the language from its first word after them
# (codeblock.js), so the label still embeds.

``` memetic-wikitext
<<~ stance named=`poet`>>
#   ^^^^^^ keyword.control.sigil.memetic-wikitext
```

# A SEVEN-TICK FENCE keeps its label's grammar past a paired inner six-tick fence, and closes only at seven.

```````memetic-wikitext
``````text
inner, read raw
``````
<<~ stance named=`poet`>>
#   ^^^^^^ keyword.control.sigil.memetic-wikitext
```````
#<- punctuation.definition.raw.markup.end.tiddlywiki5
